1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:01,920
Mark 16

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:08,760
When the Sabbath was passed, Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of James and Salome

3
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:11,900
bought spices so that they might go and anoint him.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:17,720
And very early on the first day of the week, when the sun had risen, they went to the tomb,

5
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,880
and they were saying to one another,

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:24,460
Who will roll away the stone for us from the entrance of the tomb?

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,220
And looking up, they saw that the stone had been rolled back. It was very large.

8
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:36,120
And entering the tomb, they saw a young man sitting on the right side dressed in a white robe,

9
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,980
and they were alarmed. And he said to them,

10
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:44,060
Do not be alarmed. You seek Jesus of Nazareth, who was crucified.

11
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:49,540
He has risen. He is not here. See the place where they laid him?

12
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,280
But go, tell his disciples and Peter,

13
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:54,440
that he is going to the tomb.

14
00:00:54,460 --> 00:01:00,120
He will point before you to Galilee. There you will see him, just as he told you.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,820
And they went out and fled from the tomb, for trembling and astonishment had seized them,

16
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,740
and they said nothing to anyone, for they were afraid.

17
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:12,900
Now when he rose early on the first day of the week,

18
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,280
he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom he had cast out seven demons.

19
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:22,200
She went and told those who had been with him, as they mourned and wept.

20
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,200
But when they heard that he was alive,

21
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:27,260
and had been seen by her, they would not believe it.

22
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:31,740
After these things he appeared in another form to two of them,

23
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,580
as they were walking into the country.

24
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,260
And they went back and told the rest, but they did not believe them.

25
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:42,840
Afterward he appeared to the eleven themselves, as they were reclining at table,

26
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,540
and he rebuked them for their unbelief and hardness of heart,

27
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:50,080
because they had not believed those who saw him after he had risen.

28
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,120
And he said to them,

29
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:54,240
Go into all the world,

30
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:56,620
and proclaim the gospel to the whole creation.

31
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,740
Whoever believes and is baptized will be saved,

32
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,480
but whoever does not believe will be condemned.

33
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:05,980
And these signs will accompany those who believe.

34
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,180
In my name they will cast out demons,

35
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,140
they will speak in new tongues,

36
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:13,480
they will pick up serpents with their hands,

37
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:16,680
and if they drink any deadly poison, it will not hurt them.

38
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:21,020
They will lay their hands on the sick, and they will recover.

39
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:24,020
So then the Lord Jesus, after he had spoken,

40
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:28,860
was taken up into heaven and sat down at the right hand of God.

41
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:33,480
And they went out and preached everywhere while the Lord worked with them

42
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,300
and confirmed the message by accompanying signs.

